# Contact form spam protection

## Use Cases

- Changing the public contact form, recaptcha, or contact mailables.
- Adding another page that posts to `contact-submit`.

## Constraints

- Every contact form must include `partials.contact-guard-fields` and `partials.contact-recaptcha-script`.
- Verify reCAPTCHA v3 success, `action=contact`, hostname, and score `>= config('contact.recaptcha_min_score')`.
- Honeypot `company_url` filled → fake success, send no mail.
- Encrypted `form_ts` must be 3s–1h old.
- Reject more than `config('contact.max_urls')` `http(s)` links.
- Mail admin only (`config('contact.admin_email')`). Do not auto-reply to the submitter (open relay).
- Do not put `contact@` in Reply-To or page HTML.
- Do not mention `otscommunity.com`.

## Valid Examples

```php
Mail::to(config('contact.admin_email'))->queue(new ContactForAdminMail(...));
```

```blade
@include('partials.contact-guard-fields')
```

## Invalid Examples

```php
Mail::to($request->input('email'))->queue(new ContactMail(...));
Mail::to('ots.for.work@gmail.com')->queue(...); // hard-code
```

```blade
<input type="hidden" name="g-recaptcha-response"> {{-- without honeypot + form_ts --}}
```
